 ## Background
 
-Marching Tetrahedra was introduced in 1991 by Doi and Koide as a crack-free, historically patent-free alternative to Marching Cubes [S4, unofficial]. It resolves the 15 ambiguous cases of Marching Cubes by decomposing the cube into tetrahedra, each of which has a unique intersection topology [S3, S4, unofficial].
+Marching Tetrahedra was introduced in 1991 by Doi and Koide as a crack-free, historically patent-free alternative to Marching Cubes [S5, unofficial]. It resolves the 15 ambiguous cases of Marching Cubes by decomposing the cube into tetrahedra, each of which has a unique intersection topology [S3, S4, unofficial]. It is employed in dynamic isosurface rendering of unstructured data [S7, unofficial].
 
